PART 7: ROUTE PARAMETERS AND CONSTRAINTS
============================================================

28. REQUIRED PARAMETER

Syntax:

Route::get('/employees/{id}', function ($id) {
    return "Employee ID: {$id}";
});

URL:

/employees/25

Output:

Employee ID: 25


29. MULTIPLE PARAMETERS

Syntax:

Route::get(
    '/departments/{department}/employees/{employee}',
    function ($department, $employee) {
        return "Department: {$department}, Employee: {$employee}";
    }
);

Example URL:

/departments/3/employees/25


30. OPTIONAL PARAMETER

Syntax:

Route::get('/employees/{name?}', function ($name = null) {
    return $name ?? 'All Employees';
});

Examples:

/employees
/employees/Rahul

The question mark makes the parameter optional.

Give the corresponding argument a default value.


31. NUMERIC CONSTRAINT

Syntax:

Route::get('/employees/{id}', function ($id) {
    return $id;
})->whereNumber('id');


32. ALPHABETIC CONSTRAINT

Syntax:

Route::get('/employees/{name}', function ($name) {
    return $name;
})->whereAlpha('name');


33. ALPHANUMERIC CONSTRAINT

Syntax:

Route::get('/departments/{department}', function ($department) {
    return $department;
})->whereAlphaNumeric('department');


34. CUSTOM REGULAR EXPRESSION

Syntax:

Route::get('/employees/{id}', function ($id) {
    return $id;
})->where('id', '[0-9]+');


35. CONSTRAIN MULTIPLE PARAMETERS

Syntax:

Route::get(
    '/employees/{employee}/projects/{project}',
    function ($employee, $project) {
        return 'Employee and Project';
    }
)->where([
    'employee' => '[0-9]+',
    'project' => '[0-9]+',
]);


36. GLOBAL ROUTE PARAMETER PATTERN

File:

app/Providers/AppServiceProvider.php

Inside the boot() method:

use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Route;

public function boot(): void
{
    Route::pattern('id', '[0-9]+');
}

This constrains route parameters named id across routes.

IMPORTANT:

A route constraint checks the URL parameter's format.

It does not prove that a database record exists or that the current user is authorized to access it.


